WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.658
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will represent apparatus, crews, and

00:00:05.658 --> 00:00:11.315
gps devices. A vehicle name alone does not tell a dispatcher its type,

00:00:11.315 --> 00:00:16.973
home station, crew, or location source. We will explain the features, the setup

00:00:16.973 --> 00:00:20.890
decisions, and a practical way to check the result.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:26.289
Engine 1 and Rescue 1 are added with their unit types and assigned

00:00:26.289 --> 00:00:31.088
to Station 1. Units let dispatchers send the right resources and let everyone

00:00:31.088 --> 00:00:35.887
see which apparatus is available. The examples in this series use a fictional

00:00:35.887 --> 00:00:38.840
department and are teaching scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:45.045
Units. Your apparatus, vehicles and response teams. Add each unit with its type

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.770
and home station group.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:53.158
Unit types. Categories such as Engine, Ladder or Ambulance. Create unit types before

00:00:53.158 --> 00:00:56.720
adding units so each unit can be classified.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:03.430
Hardware location tracking. GPS devices that report unit locations. Register each tracking device

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.250
and link it to its unit.

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:12.095
New Unit. Add an apparatus, vehicle or team. List your apparatus or response

00:01:12.095 --> 00:01:17.339
teams with their types and home stations. Teams that respond only as individuals

00:01:17.339 --> 00:01:19.760
can mark this module not applicable.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:25.686
Unit Staffing. Assign crew members to units. List your apparatus or response teams

00:01:25.686 --> 00:01:31.012
with their types and home stations. Teams that respond only as individuals can

00:01:31.012 --> 00:01:33.060
mark this module not applicable.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:39.117
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Create Engine and

00:01:39.117 --> 00:01:44.574
Rescue unit types. Step 2. Add Engine 1 with its type, Station 1,

00:01:44.574 --> 00:01:50.031
and crew roles. Step 3. Assign the crew and, when used, register a

00:01:50.031 --> 00:01:52.130
tracking device against the unit.

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:58.603
Now verify the result. Confirm the unit type, home station, crew, and status.

00:01:58.603 --> 00:02:04.477
For hardware tracking, check a recent received position and the stale-position behavior. A

00:02:04.477 --> 00:02:10.350
common problem to watch for: An old GPS position is not a live

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:15.320
position. Crew assignment, reported unit status, and physical readiness are distinct.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.884
Your practice task is simple. Create Engine 1 in the demo department and

00:02:20.884 --> 00:02:25.848
verify the assigned crew from the dispatcher view. Measure incomplete unit records. Record

00:02:25.848 --> 00:02:30.812
the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed. Use

00:02:30.812 --> 00:02:34.630
the linked feature scripts for the detailed screen recording plan.

